# Pin of the cream executor used by the checks of this catalog: cream validate
# (tools/cream-validate.sh), the catalog snapshot (tools/cream-deb.sh) and the
# live runs (tools/live-test.sh). Plain KEY=value lines, read by the scripts
# without sourcing. This file is the only place of the version: raising cream
# is one edit here (and the `cream:` of the extensions that need the new one).
#
# CREAM_VERSION — release version without "v"; CREAM_SHA256 — sha256 of
# cream_<version>_amd64.deb from that release (what the tools run: CI and the
# hosts are amd64). CREAM_SHA256_ARM64 — sha256 of cream_<version>_arm64.deb,
# the same release on record (no tool takes it yet). Both sums come from the
# release's SHA256SUMS:
#   gh release download v<version> -R iamletenkov/cream -p SHA256SUMS
# CREAM_VERSION and CREAM_SHA256 both empty means "no cream release yet": the
# check is skipped with a line, not failed. One of them without the other is an
# error. CREAM_URL (optional) — where to take the .deb; empty means the GitHub
# release asset of iamletenkov/cream.
#
# 1.1.0: stages early/cloud-user/graphical, `cream validate --catalog` graph.
# Its stage cloud-user does not start with cloud-init disabled — fixed in 1.1.1;
# ruling R14: tools/lint-hooks.sh asks such a manifest for cream: ">=1.1.1".
# 1.1.1: cloud-user without cloud-init, system init without the extra lock.
# 1.1.2: validate.unit_lock warns only about a real deadlock (no false alarms on teleport).
CREAM_VERSION=1.1.2
CREAM_SHA256=bde00fafaaa4bf7447e6c3cfb96e7ef639a2f1fdc997f79a13e82a9d79220780
CREAM_SHA256_ARM64=9c42d1fa7a02371839ef864ea0d29b454cdf3342f0e6a4f66c40cf077c325c44
CREAM_URL=
